OL,3,GNEWSAIndia bowled over by cricket bats
OL,4,Amade in Suffolk
OL,5,
OL,6,FFrom an English woodland to a cricket
OL,7,Ffield half the world away, tens of
OL,8,Fthousands of cricket bats are being
OL,9,Fshipped to India each year.
OL,11,FIt all starts with the English willow
OL,12,Ftree, commonly known as a cricket bat
OL,13,Fwillow. Manufacturers in the east of
OL,14,FEngland say the region has the perfect
OL,15,Fconditions for the tree to thrive.
OL,17,FJS Wright & Sons, which is based in
OL,18,FChelmsford, Essex, said around 75% of
OL,19,Fits products were sent to India and
OL,20,FPakistan. For Foskett Willows in
OL,21,FBromeswell, Suffolk, that figure is
OL,22,Fcloser to 90%.
OL,23,APub: 12-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB E Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
